.Dd October 15, 2026
.Dt AGVTOOL 1
.Os
.\"
.Sh NAME
.Nm agvtool
.Nd Apple-generic versioning tool for Xcode projects
.\"
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Li what-version
|
.Li vers
.Op Fl terse
.Nm
.Op Fl noscm | Fl usecvs | Fl usesvn
.Li next-version
|
.Li bump
.Op Fl all
.Nm
.Op Fl noscm | Fl usecvs | Fl usesvn
.Li new-version
.Op Fl all
.Ar versionNumber
.Nm
.Op Fl noscm | Fl usecvs | Fl usesvn
.Li tag
.Op Fl force | Fl F
.Op Fl noupdatecheck | Fl Q
.Op Fl baseurlfortag
.Nm
.Op Fl noscm | Fl usecvs | Fl usesvn
.Li submit
.Op Fl bytag | Fl notbytag
.Op Fl baseurlfortag
.Ar release ...
.Nm
.Li what-marketing-version
|
.Li mvers
.Op Fl terse | Fl terse1
.Nm
.Op Fl noscm | Fl usecvs | Fl usesvn
.Li new-marketing-version
.Ar version
.\"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
speeds up common operations for Xcode projects that use the Apple-generic
versioning system.
.Pp
Versioning support is enabled by setting some build settings in your project.
.\"
.Ss Build Settings
.Bl -tag -width "VERSION_INFO_EXPORT_DECL"
.It Li VERSIONING_SYSTEM
Must be set to
.Dq apple-generic
at the project level to enable versioning.
.It Li CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION
The current version of the project. The value must be an integer or floating
point number such as 57 or 365.8.
.It Li DYLIB_CURRENT_VERSION
The current version of any framework built by the project. Like
.Li CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION
the value must be an integer or floating point number. By default it is set to
.Dq $(CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION) Ns .
.It Li VERSION_INFO_PREFIX
A prefix for the name of the version info symbol in the generated versioning
source file.
.It Li VERSION_INFO_SUFFIX
A suffix for the name of the version info symbol. This is rarely used.
.It Li VERSION_INFO_BUILDER
A reference to the user performing a build to be included in the generated
stub; defaults to the value of the
.Ev USER
environment variable.
.It Li VERSION_INFO_EXPORT_DECL
A prefix string for the version info symbol declaration in the generated stub.
This should rarely be changed.
.It Li VERSION_INFO_FILE
The name of the source file that is generated and compiled into your product.
By default this is
.Dq $(PRODUCT_NAME)_vers.c Ns .
.El
.Pp
To enable Apple-generic versioning you must set up at least the
.Li VERSIONING_SYSTEM
and
.Li CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION
project build settings for each project you want to be versioned.
.Pp
Projects with multiple targets are required to have the same
.Li CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION
for each target. The easiest way to achieve this is to set
.Li CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION
at the project level.
.\"
.Ss Usage
.Nm
should be invoked with the working directory set to your project directory
(the folder containing your .xcodeproj project file).
.Pp
.Nm
pays attention to the following defaults for CVS usage:
.Li CVSEnabled ,
.Li CVSSubmitByTag ,
and
.Li CVSToolPath .
.Pp
If
.Li CVSEnabled
is set to
.Li YES
then
.Nm
performs certain CVS operations such as committing modified project files and
performing tagging operations. The sense of this default can be overridden by
supplying an explicit
.Fl noscm
(turns off CVS and Subversion usage),
.Fl usecvs
(turns on CVS usage and turns off Subversion usage),
or
.Fl usesvn
(turns off CVS usage and turns on Subversion usage).
.Pp
If
.Li CVSSubmitByTag
is set to
.Li YES
then
.Nm
submits your project by CVS tag using the same version as the tag operation.
The sense of this default can be overridden with
.Fl bytag
or
.Fl notbytag
on the submit operation.
.Pp
Set
.Li CVSToolPath
to point to the location of the cvs tool to use. If this default is not set
then
.Nm
uses
.Pa /usr/bin/ocvs
if it exists, otherwise
.Pa /usr/bin/cvs .
.Pp
.Nm
pays attention to the following defaults for Subversion usage:
.Li SVNEnabled ,
.Li SVNSubmitByTag ,
and
.Li SVNToolPath .
.Pp
If
.Li SVNEnabled
is set to
.Li YES
then
.Nm
performs certain Subversion operations such as committing modified project
files and performing tagging operations. The sense of this default can be
overridden as described above.
.Pp
If
.Li SVNSubmitByTag
is set to
.Li YES
then
.Nm
submits your project by Subversion URL using the same version as that created
by the tag operation.
.Pp
Set
.Li SVNToolPath
to point to the location of the svn tool to use. If this default is not set
then
.Nm
uses
.Pa /usr/local/bin/svn
if it exists.
.\"
.Ss Commands And Options
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Li what-version No | Li vers Op Fl terse
Prints out the current version number of the project.
.Pp
The
.Fl terse
option limits the output to the version number only.
.It Li next-version No | Li bump Op Fl all
Increments the version numbers of all versioned targets to the next highest
integral value. For example, 54 changes to 55 and 234.6 changes to 235.
.Pp
The
.Li CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION
and the
.Li DYLIB_CURRENT_VERSION
are updated. The
.Fl all
option also updates the
.Li CFBundleVersion
Info.plist key.
.Pp
If CVS support is enabled, the modified project file is committed.
.It Li new-version Op Fl all Ar version
Sets the version numbers of all targets to the given version.
.Pp
The
.Li CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION
and the
.Li DYLIB_CURRENT_VERSION
are updated. The
.Fl all
option also updates the
.Li CFBundleVersion
Info.plist key.
.Pp
If CVS support is enabled, the modified project file is committed.
.It Li tag Oo Fl force | Fl F Oc Oo Fl noupdatecheck | Fl Q Oc Oo Fl baseurlfortag Oc
Creates a new tag
.Ar projectname Ns - Ns Ar currentversion
where
.Ar projectname
is the name of the Xcode project file (without the extension) and
.Ar currentversion
is the
.Li CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION
with any
.Sq \&.
transformed into
.Sq ~
(since CVS does not allow dots in tag names).
.Pp
The
.Fl force
or
.Fl F
option adds a
.Fl F
to the tag operation.
.Pp
The
.Fl noupdatecheck
or
.Fl Q
option skips the cvs update usually done prior to tagging to ensure that there
are no uncommitted changes.
.Pp
The
.Fl baseurlfortag
option provides a URL that points to the directory to place the tag in when
using Subversion. This overrides the
.Li SVNBaseTagURL
default and is ignored if Subversion is not being used.
.Pp
.Em Note:
This command only functions if CVS or Subversion support is enabled.
.It Li submit Oo Fl bytag | Fl notbytag Oc Oo Fl baseurlfortag Oc Ar release ...
Submits your project to the specified releases in Build & Integration.
.Pp
The
.Fl bytag
option performs the submission by tag instead of submitting from the project
source directly. The
.Fl notbytag
option submits from the project source.
.Pp
If
.Li CVSSubmitByTag
is set,
.Fl bytag
is the default; otherwise
.Fl notbytag
is the default.
.Pp
The
.Fl baseurlfortag
option provides a URL that points to the directory to find tags in when using
Subversion. This overrides the
.Li SVNBaseTagURL
default and is ignored if Subversion is not being used.
.Pp
.Em Note:
This command is relevant only for Apple employees.
.It Li what-marketing-version No | Li mvers Op Fl terse | Fl terse1
Prints the current marketing version of the project. For native targets, a
marketing version is listed for each Info.plist file found.
.Pp
The marketing version is the
.Li CFBundleShortVersionString
Info.plist key. This is often a totally different version determined by
product marketing.
.Pp
The
.Fl terse
option limits the output to the version number only.
.Pp
The
.Fl terse1
option limits the output to the first version number found, and only displays
the version number.
.It Li new-marketing-version Ar version
Sets the marketing version numbers of all versioned targets to the given
version number.
.Pp
The marketing version is the
.Li CFBundleShortVersionString
Info.plist key.
.Pp
If CVS support is enabled, the modified project file is committed.
.Pp
Do not use this command on a project with targets that track different
marketing versions.
.El
.\"
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits with one of the following values:
.Bl -tag -width 4n -offset indent
.It 0
Success.
.It 2
A command was given an invalid argument or option.
.It 3
.Nm
was not run from a directory containing exactly one Xcode project.
.It 7
The requested version could not be set.
.El
